{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566909-character-rolling-roundtable","id":566909,"title":"Character Rolling Roundtable","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T14:05:35-07:00","id":566909,"title":"Character Rolling Roundtable","content":"Ah, the character sheet. The thing no one *else* at the table cares about, as long as you use dice pools large enough to get by. But you, you slaved over that thing. Mused the philosophical impact of taking four whole dots of stamina at character generation. The narrative restrictions of three dots in firearms, even though your character hasn't been any closer to a firefight than playing Call of Duty.<br /> <br /> Nothing is more boring than hearing Bob drone on about what skills he put points in, but the character sheet ties your wild ideas to in-game mechanics. Doing it properly means you *can* do the things you *want* to do.<br /> <br /> So I figured, hey, why don't we talk about the awesome things we want characters to accomplish, and suggest ways to map that out on paper? There is plenty more to the concept 'legendary pit fighter' than slapping five dots each in strength and brawl and calling it a day, right?<br /> <br /> For example: what if you wanted to make an Uratha who was... <br /> <br /> Training to be an Olympic athlete before their Change?<br /> <br /> Just off the top of my head, I would say its more than dots in Athletics - maybe their trainer means they should have a dot in mentor, and they have been dragged to enough fundraisers and cocktail parties to have some grip on Politics and Socialize as well. And of course they had to go to a great school with that scholarship, so polish up those Academics while you are at it...<br /> <br /> Anyone have better ideas? Or an idea of their own to float by?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T17:14:03-07:00","id":567135,"title":"","content":"I actually really enjoy analyzing character stats, I love when my friends tell me about the neat synergies they built into their character sheet, or the background behind why they have X dots in Y trait.<br /> <br /> For the Olympic athlete question, it depends on the sport. I think 4 dots of Athletics is a given, but if they were training to be a track runner you'd probably want a few dots of Fleet of Foot, whereas if they were training to be a champion on the uneven bars, you might want Double Jointed. Depending on their relationship with their trainer, they might make their trainer their first Flesh Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T19:27:52-07:00","id":567252,"title":"","content":"*Points out Chess is an Olympic sport.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T19:49:54-07:00","id":567262,"title":"","content":"They might have one or two dots of Medicine representing the knowledge of their own bodies and of first aid that they've acquired. If they were Olympic level and actually competed, that's at LEAST grounds for Fame 1, if not 2 or 3 depending upon how they did and what kind of personality they have.<br /> <br /> They might have Resources from promoting products and stuff, if they're one of those big names.<br /> <br /> They probably have little to no dots in Brawl. Why? Your body is a temple! Getting into fights and risking injury is one of <i>the worst things </i>an Olympian can do. (It doesn't stop it from happening, but when everything you've worked for is on the line, the risk of anything like that is clear) A lot of them (a lot of athletes in general) sign contracts that expressly forbid them from doing certain kinds of dangerous things, usually with fines attached to them. So that's something to keep in mind too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-24-2015, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T19:56:58-07:00","id":567265,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely say a couple dots in Medicine for the dieting and possible doping (yes, I'm a cynic). Probably a couple in Subterfuge for keeping it from the family. That does depend on the sport, of course. Might want Iron Stamina instead of Fleet of Foot if you're a marathon runner and not a sprinter. Double Jointed makes a lot of sense for a gymnast. Any sort of runner probably has fast reflexes (Unless you're one of those slow starters who make up for it with a long stride *cough*UsainBolt*endcough*)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:53:13-07:00","id":567386,"title":"","content":"Ooh! All good ideas. Let me try another one, if you don't mind. How would you represent an Uratha who...<br /> <br /> ...comes from a big, old, 'in the know' wolf-blooded family? (Like, if the Weasleys were werewolves? Weresleys?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}